+\subsection{Qualitative Prediction Examples}
+\label{sec:qualitative-predictions}
+
+The prediction panels supplement the aggregate comparisons with examples
+of where models agree with or depart from the reference. They use fresh
+matched reproductions, because the original final adapters and prediction
+volumes were not retained. For each pretrained-model study, the constrained
+objective is the one with the highest original mean validation Dice.
+The reproduced run pair was chosen before execution as the pair with the
+median original gain among the nine recorded comparisons. Thus, each
+dataset contributes one baseline and one constrained reproduction, rather
+than a new three-fold, three-seed study.
+
+The repeats preserve the recorded support and validation cases,
+initial weights, sampling sequence and update schedule. SAM3 uses five
+GeoFWI3D support volumes and 25 updates; MedSAM3 uses five MSD volumes or
+two ADNI crops and 200 updates. Medical runs reuse the saved calibration
+coefficients. The geological runs repeat the original five-update
+calibration procedure. Inference uses images and the fixed text queries;
+reference masks enter evaluation and figure selection, not the model's
+inference prompts. Case identities, reference hashes and final-adapter
+identities were checked, and Dice and error counts were recalculated from
+all 416 saved support and validation predictions.
+
+\begin{table}[htbp]
+\centering\small\setstretch{1.05}
+\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.2}
+\begin{tabular}{@{}lrrrrr@{}}
+\hline
+& \multicolumn{2}{c}{Original run pair} &
+\multicolumn{3}{c}{Qualitative reproduction} \\
+Study (held-out cases) & Baseline & Constrained & Baseline & Constrained & $\Delta$ \\
+\hline
+GeoFWI3D / SAM3 (96) & 75.39 & 78.21 & 76.72 & 79.47 & +2.75 \\
+MSD / MedSAM3 (46) & 77.55 & 82.47 & 78.63 & 81.87 & +3.24 \\
+ADNI / MedSAM3 (54) & 78.02 & 81.57 & 77.12 & 80.64 & +3.52 \\
+\hline
+\end{tabular}
+\caption{Mean foreground Dice for the selected original run pairs and
+their qualitative reproductions. Scores are percentages and $\Delta$ is
+the reproduced paired gain in percentage points, calculated before
+rounding. These are single-run validation means, not the original
+three-fold aggregates. Constrained objectives follow
+Figure~\ref{fig:qualitative-typical}.}
+\label{tab:qualitative-reproduction-scores}
+\end{table}
+
+The repetitions are not numerically identical to the original runs
+(Table~\ref{tab:qualitative-reproduction-scores}). The largest change in
+paired gain occurs on MSD: 4.93 points in the selected original pair
+becomes 3.24 points. Training records already diverge at the first update,
+before inference, despite matching initial weights and sampling. On
+GeoFWI3D and ADNI the first forward losses agree but gradient norms differ;
+on MSD the baseline forward losses also differ. The recorded MSD hardware
+changes from a full A100-SXM4 GPU to an A100 PCIe GPU partition. These
+checks locate the divergence in optimization but do not establish its
+exact numerical cause. Repeating geological calibration also changes
+the edge and depth coefficients. The panels therefore describe the
+reproduced models and do not stand in for the original predictions.
+
+For each reproduced validation set, cases are ordered by constrained
+minus baseline whole-volume Dice, with case identifier breaking ties.
+The upper-median case is shown in Figure~\ref{fig:qualitative-typical};
+the minimum and maximum changes are shown below. The same predetermined
+slice rule applies to all examples: choose the first slice along source
+array axis two, indexed from zero, with the largest reference foreground
+area. Images, views, intensity limits and label colours are identical
+within each pair. These are stored-grid views, with no anatomical-plane
+claim. Scores describe entire volumes, so the displayed slice need not
+contain the errors responsible for the largest part of a score change.
+
+The constrained reproduction improves Dice in 88 of 96 GeoFWI3D volumes,
+41 of 46 MSD crops and 51 of 54 ADNI crops. The exceptions make the limits
+of the average improvement concrete. In the adverse geological case,
+whole-volume false positives rise from 4,981 to 7,947, while false
+negatives fall only from 911 to 773. The selected slice lies on the cube
+face and shows only part of that error balance. In the adverse MSD case,
+false positives rise from 188 to 645 despite fewer missed voxels and
+anterior/posterior swaps. In the adverse ADNI case, both missed and extra
+foreground increase. These examples support the need to examine the
+kind and location of errors alongside Dice; they provide no assessment
+of clinical or geological usefulness.
+
